nk a mace into a northern  colleague instantly this makes the  conniving mage a traitor but to what end  well in the second season vilgefortz is  vying for a seat on the council in  aratuza together with tesea the two make  a compelling team and it's revealed that  they now share an intimate relationship  tris returns to aratuza and tells to say  of series significance and then tasaya  betrays her confidence sharing this info  with vilgefortz upon learning of siri  vilgefortz is adamant that she is  pursued ultimately the brotherhood puts  a bounty on her head and on anyone  attempting to protect her vilgefortz  clearly has a hidden allegiance or  agenda but it remains to be seen what  the full scope of his intentions are as  he seemingly manipulates his colleagues  to his own ends  for a time siri was so in awe of  geralt's prowess in the realm of rooting  out and defeating monsters that she  became hell-bent on becoming a witcher  herself the only problem with that idea  is that the formula for creating the  witcher mutagen had been destroyed long  ago rendering them incapable of making  more witchers however when tris reveals  that siri has elder blood vesimir's hope  is renewed he asks siri's permission to  begin creating the mutagen once again  siri agrees on one condition she gets  the first taste while becoming a witcher  requires vigorous training the most  crucial element is the mutation they  undergo that refines their senses  reflexes and strength unfortunately most  witcher candidates die during the trial  of the grasses the process of receiving  the alchemical concoction to undergo the  necessary changes siri is willing to  take the risk but geralt is not he stops  her from making perhaps one of the  greatest mistakes she could possibly  make however the question remains what  would have happened had siri actually  taken the mutagen it's clear that there  are no female witchers that occupy  karamorin would siri have become the  first  while at karamorin tris uses her magic  to take siri on a trip through a  dreamscape that triss is seemingly in  control of by the end however triss  begins to fear as the visages of people  within the dreamscape actually see her  something that isn't supposed to occur  furthermore siri gets her first view of  the wild hunt a pack of wraiths who  appear as ghostly specters of death upon  horses when the two emerge from the  dreamscape tris fears siri and claims  that she'll destroy everything in fleas  all throughout season 2 many people are  telling siri who she is and what she can  become trista's view was the only one  that stemmed from fear of the centron  princess possibly bringing about the  apocalypse will siri fulfill triss's  fears of death and destruction only time  will tell  frangilla francesca and jennifer all  encountered the woman in the hut who  manipulated them and fed off their pain  in despair known as the voleth mare she  bargained with yennefer to bring her  siri in exchange for the restoration of  her chaos aka her magic yennefer came to  her senses as she bonded with siri and  understood her importance however it was  too late as voleth mayor fed off the  pain and anguish that francesca felt  over the loss of her murdered child  which released her from the hut that the  first witchers had previously banished  her to ultimately it was revealed that  she wanted siri because the princess was  the only one who could return her home  to her own sphere where she shares a  home with the wild hunt while we are  sure to see more of the wild hunt in the  future will we be seeing more of volath  mare as well  the big reveal at the end of season 2 is  that the leader of nilfgaard emperor  emir varem reyes is actually siri's  father dooney who supposedly died years  ago while fleeing sintra the netflix  series hasn't made clear what really  happened to siri's parents but we do  know that dooney is actually emperor  emir emir states his intent of finding  siri but why did he leave her in the  first place what really happened to  princess pavetta it's likely that the  next season will shed more light on amir  and his history between the time that he  was protected by geralt and his present  status as ruler of nilfgaard  there are several questions that now  emerge with the reveal of emperor emir  sure he seemingly abandoned his daughter  for many years but why is he a sworn  enemy of sintra and the northern  kingdoms what does his conquest truly  afford him sentra was the home of his  beloved princess pavetta who he fell  madly in love with he risked his life  for her hand in marriage and they of  course had a daughter after managing to  claim leadership over nilfgaard why then  would he destroy sintra resulting in the  deaths of his mother-in-law queen  kalanthi and potentially cause harm to  his daughter siri in the first season  dooney seemed timid yet honorable he  claimed to have once saved the life of  the king of sentra which granted him the  law of surprise nothing in dooney's  nature ever indicated he was a  bloodthirsty tyrant willing to kill  babies to sow chaos what exactly  happened to dooney after all these years  that turned him into the dreaded emperor  of nilfgaard  series elderblood offered vessemir a  chance at restoring the witcher order  destiny has given us a gift  the key to making more witches  he created his first batch of mutagens  with her help and was prepared to put  siri through the trial of the grasses in  order to fulfill her wish of becoming a  witcher even if it could have  potentially killed her however if siri  ever decided to donate blood again to  the witcher cause they could potentially  create even more will vesemir and his  witcher brothers at karamorin begin  training and finding new potential  candidates for witchers once again it  seems that it's now within their  capability to do so but it may not be  within serious destiny to participate in  the witcher resurgence we'll have to  wait and see what the future holds for  the witcher order in the next season  in the climactic moments of season 2 a  silent assassin kills philip andrel and  francesca's child and in a horrifying  act of vengeance the elves go on a quest  to ridania where they repay the crimes  committed toward them a hundredfold  francesca uses magic to slaughter the  babies of redania in a vile act that  could threaten the standing of the elves  in the world order even further the  birth of francesca's child ultimately  swayed the elves to rebuild instead of  going to war for nilfgaard because of  this their child was murdered so that  once again they become pawns in  nilfgaard's game of conquest but now  they threaten everything they've worked  for by sullying their name with the  actions committed in redania and we  wonder what kind of consequences they're  going to face in season three  geralt and jennifer are two of the most  prominent characters in the entire  series and they're known for their  passionate romance and feelings toward  one another something geralt never  exhibited previously but now geralt is  faced with jennifer's betrayal as she'd  planned to offer siri up to the  deathless mother in exchange for  restoring her magic while jennifer  didn't go through with her plan in the  end the moment still cut geralt rather  deeply  i know i've heard you  yet i can't help but wish you can begin  again  in the end he tells jennifer that he  can't forgive her however he needs her  to train siri and help her hone her  abilities can geralt find it in his  heart to move past a moment of bad  judgment after all he knows what it's  like to feel empty inside and without  purpose if the history of these two  characters has taught us anything it's  that they'll surely find their way back  to each other once again  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite shows are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don